Account of Yadvendradas of Agra, Disciple of Shri Gusainji

Yadvendradas lived in Agra and remained close to Shri Gusainji. He had memorized every line of Shri Subodhiniji and immersed himself day and night in the divine Leela. By the power of divine rasa, he attained sakhi-bhav and became qualified to behold all the sacred Leelas.

One day, he beheld Shri Gusainji together with Shri Govardhannathji in the Divine Couple (Yugal) form, just as Gopaldasji sang in his Akhyan:

Though one in essence, the two forms manifest distinctly to perform manifold Leelas and blissful communion;
Through tender exchanges of words and glances, they signal the delights of the nocturnal pastime. (1)
Adorned with varied pearl necklaces strung on silk threads, gleaming beautifully around Their necks;
With garlands of diverse blossoms woven by Their own hands, They affectionately place garlands around one another's necks. (2)
Offering manifold dried fruits, sweet delicacies, and rich flavors in countless ways;
And fragrant betel-leaf beedas spiced with camphor, cardamom, cloves, betel nut, and catechu. (3)

Such transcendent visions were granted to Yadvendradasji by Shri Gusainji's grace. Whatever visions he beheld, he composed and sang as fresh devotional pads. Such a supremely favored Kshatriya disciple of Shri Gusainji was Yadvendradas.
